==Serbo-Croatian==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|sh|sla-pro|*ljudije||people, men}},from {{etyl|ine-bsl-pro|sh}} {{m|ine-bsl-pro|*leudeiěs||people, men}} from {{etyl|ine-pro|sh}} {{m|ine-pro|*h₁lewdʰ-}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ʎûːdi/|lang=sh}}
* {{hyphenation|lju|di|lang=sh}}

===Noun===
{{sh-noun|g=m|head=ljȗdi}} (singular: {{l|sh|čȍvjek}} / {{l|sh|čȍvek}})

# [[people]], [[men]]
#: Dva ''čovjeka'' su išla cestom — ''Two '''men''' walked down the street.''
#: Pet ''ljudi'' je išlo cestom. — ''Five '''people''' walked down the street.''

====Usage notes====
This plural form takes suppletive stem in the singular, as can be seen in the declension table. Old dual forms have been preserved in the counting for 2, 3, 4 (also for 22, 23, 24, 32, 33, 34, etc., whereas the singular form is used for 21, 31, 41, etc.) which bind plural form of {{m|sh|čȍvjek}} / {{m|sh|čȍvek}}.

